  "line": "Jerusalem is the city David captured and made his capital, where the temple stood, where Jesus was welcomed as King, and where the Holy Spirit came upon the believers.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "David Takes the Fortress",
      "text": "David marched against the Jebusites, who said he could never get in. He captured the fortress of Zion and called it the City of David, and he became greater because the LORD was with him.",
      "passage": "2 Samuel 5:6-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Ark Comes to the Temple",
      "text": "Solomon gathered Israel's leaders in Jerusalem to bring the ark of the covenant to the temple. The priests placed it in the Most Holy Place, and the glory of the LORD filled the house in a cloud.",
      "passage": "1 Kings 8:1-11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Babylon Destroys the City",
      "text": "Nebuchadnezzar surrounded Jerusalem with his army and a siege wall. Later his captain burned the house of the LORD, the palace, and the houses, and the army broke down the city walls.",
      "passage": "2 Kings 25:1-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jesus Enters Jerusalem",
      "text": "Jesus rode toward Jerusalem on a donkey while crowds spread cloaks and branches and shouted, \"Hosanna to the Son of David!\" When He entered, the whole city was stirred and asked, \"Who is this?\"",
      "passage": "Matthew 21:1-11"
    },
